# Claude Code
# Ignore local Claude settings/state, but track the project's shared subagents
# (.claude/agents/ — Claude Code-specific, no canonical .agents/ analog) and the
# .claude/agent-protocols/ + .claude/skills/ symlinks pointing at their canonical
# source under .agents/ (see .agents/protocols/agent-skills.md). The mechanical
# helper/wrapper scripts formerly here now live at scripts/agent-tooling/ (moved
# 2026-07, Nethermind-style: portable, not Claude-specific, shared team tooling).
# .claude/worktrees/bin/ — the worktree lifecycle scripts, moved here (out of
# agent-protocols/worktrees/bin/) to sit next to the worktree dirs themselves, same
# layout as .claude/looping/bin/. The rest of .claude/worktrees/ (the actual worktree
# checkouts) stays untracked — those are full working trees, never committed content.
# The rest of .claude/sprints/ (QUEUE.md, patterns/, completed/, archive/, and — as of
# 2026-07-07 — log/) stays untracked/operator-local. log/ was previously tracked as a
# durable team record, but is now operator-local to avoid a stream of log-only commits
# on shared history; the sprint-lifecycle close-out still writes it, it just isn't
# committed (re-track later by removing the .claude/sprints/log/ line below if desired).
# .claude/hooks/ (comment-policy.py, advisory PostToolUse check) and the new tracked
# .claude/settings.json that wires it are shared team tooling, same as agents/skills below —
# .claude/settings.local.json stays untracked/operator-local, unaffected by this exception.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agent-protocols/
!.claude/looping/
.claude/looping/state/*/
!.claude/looping/bin/
!.claude/sprints/
.claude/sprints/QUEUE.md
.claude/sprints/patterns/
.claude/sprints/completed/
.claude/sprints/archive/
.claude/sprints/log/
!.claude/worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/*
!.claude/worktrees/bin/

